NNAAMMEE
     ttiimmeeoouutt — run a command with a time limit

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ttiimmeeoouutt [--kk _t_i_m_e | ----kkiillll--aafftteerr _t_i_m_e] [--ss _s_i_g | ----ssiiggnnaall _s_i_g]
             [--vv | ----vveerrbboossee] [----ffoorreeggrroouunndd] [----pprreesseerrvvee--ssttaattuuss] _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n
             _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_a_r_g_s _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ttiimmeeoouutt starts the _c_o_m_m_a_n_d with its _a_r_g_s.  If the _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is still run‐
     ning after _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n, it is killed.  By default, SIGTERM is sent.  The
     special _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n, zero, signifies no limit.  Therefore a signal is never
     sent if _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n is 0.

     The options are as follows:

     --kk _t_i_m_e, ----kkiillll--aafftteerr _t_i_m_e
             Send a SIGKILL signal if _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is still running after _t_i_m_e af‐
             ter the first signal was sent.

     --ss _s_i_g, ----ssiiggnnaall _s_i_g
             Specify the signal to send on timeout.  By default, SIGTERM is
             sent.

     --vv, ----vveerrbboossee
             Show information to stderr about any signal sent on timeout.

     ----ffoorreeggrroouunndd
             Do not propagate timeout to the children of _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.

     ----pprreesseerrvvee--ssttaattuuss
             Exit with the same status as _c_o_m_m_a_n_d, even if it times out and is
             killed.

DDUURRAATTIIOONN FFOORRMMAATT
     The _d_u_r_a_t_i_o_n and _t_i_m_e are non-negative integer or real (decimal) numbers,
     with an optional unit-specifying suffix.  Values without an explicit unit
     are interpreted as seconds.

     Supported unit symbols are:
           ss       seconds
           mm       minutes
           hh       hours
           dd       days

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     If the timeout was not reached, the exit status of _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is returned.

     If the timeout was reached and ----pprreesseerrvvee--ssttaattuuss is set, the exit status
     of _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is returned.  If ----pprreesseerrvvee--ssttaattuuss is not set, an exit status
     of 124 is returned.

     If an invalid parameter is passed to --ss or --kk, the exit status returned
     is 125.

     If _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is an otherwise invalid program, the exit status returned is
     126.

     If _c_o_m_m_a_n_d refers to a non-existing program, the exit status returned is
     127.

     If _c_o_m_m_a_n_d exits after receiving a signal, the exit status returned is
     the signal number plus 128.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Run sleep(1) with a time limit of 4 seconds.  Since the command completes
     in 2 seconds, the exit status is 0:

           $ timeout 4 sleep 2
           $ echo $?
           0

     Run sleep(1) for 4 seconds and terminate process after 2 seconds.  124 is
     returned since no ----pprreesseerrvvee--ssttaattuuss is used:

           $ timeout 2 sleep 4
           $ echo $?
           124

     Same as above but preserving status.  Exit status is 128 + signal number
     (15 for _S_I_G_T_E_R_M):

           $ timeout --preserve-status 2 sleep 4
           $ echo $?
           143

     Same as above but sending _S_I_G_A_L_R_M (signal number 14) instead of _S_I_G_T_E_R_M:

           $ timeout --preserve-status -s SIGALRM 2 sleep 4
           $ echo $?
           142

     Try to fetch(1) the PDF version of the FreeBSD Handbook.  Send a _S_I_G_T_E_R_M
     signal after 1 minute and send a _S_I_G_K_I_L_L signal 5 seconds later if the
     process refuses to stop:

           $ timeout -k 5s 1m fetch \
           > https://download.freebsd.org/ftp/doc/en/books/handbook/book.pdf

